Under **Section 524(1)** of the **Civil Procedure Code**, an application to the District Court to have the will of a deceased person proved must be made within **three months from the date of finding of the will**.

The application must be submitted by way of a petition and affidavit, setting out:
- The fact of the making of the will;
- The details and situation of the deceased's property;
- The heirs of the deceased to the best of the petitioner's knowledge;
- The grounds upon which the petitioner is entitled to have the will proved; and
- The capacity or character in which the petitioner claims (such as executor, administrator, legatee, or heir).

